From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 13:47:23 -0500
Subject: feat: one list of routes in Settings

Rules showed only under each Space's row, by their text alone, and the page
wrote site rules and nothing else. Settings > Stedding now has a card of its
own after Spaces, "Sites routed to Spaces" (settings-stedding-routes-card). It
holds "Open links from other apps in", moved from the Spaces card, and every
rule of stedding.spaces.routes in the order that decides, each as its kind,
its text and its Space, with a remove control named for the rule. A rule made
anywhere shows at once: the handler watches the preference.

An add row takes "Site" or "Address contains", the text and a Space, the Space
on screen first. RouteFromTyped says what the text means: a site in any form
is the site, what is no site stays in the field, which says why. Each rule is
edited where it is listed. ReplaceRoute keeps its place, and an edit that
repeats another rule drops that rule. A refused edit puts the field back.
Rules of the kinds the add row does not offer keep their kind (routing D12,
D13).

A rule naming no Space, its Space gone or none named, is listed as "No Space"
and can be removed or given a Space. RoutesFromValue dropped one with an empty
Space on sight, and the next write lost it; now it is read, and RouteFor passes
over it. The card's Spaces are the registry's, so a Blank Window names rules as
any window does (routing D14).

Each Space's row in the Spaces card loses its sites and its add field: this
card is the one place. A Space with no switch to show draws no second line
(settings T9, T48, T57).

Why: people from Arc look for one list of routes and did not find it. Seen on
r/Stedding, 2026-11-05 (BACKLOG S-422, S-126).

Removable when: never as behaviour.
